<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Native AOT / Trimmer root descriptor for ZenStates.Core (net8.0-windows).

  Add types here that are loaded dynamically (e.g. via reflection, Activator.CreateInstance,
  Type.GetType, or COM interop) so the linker does not trim them away.

  NOTE ON SYNTAX: the descriptor format does not support a namespace-prefix wildcard. A
  `fullname="ZenStates.Core.*"` entry matches no type at all, so the previous version of this
  file rooted nothing and the reflection-driven paths below were silently trimmable. Only an
  exact type name, or `preserve="all"` on the <assembly> element, has any effect.

  The whole assembly is preserved because this is a library whose consumers reflect into it,
  and because several internal paths resolve members by name at runtime:

    * BaseDramTimings.this[string] resolves every DRAM timing property by name
      (GetType().GetProperty) on each read. If those properties are trimmed, GetProperty
      returns null, the caller's null check fails quietly, and every timing reads as unset
      with no exception and no warning.
    * Utils.CreateFromByteArray and Utils.ConvertValue reflect over property names and
      conversion operators of types supplied at runtime.
    * AodData and ApobData are populated by name from byte arrays.

  If assembly-wide preservation becomes too costly for binary size, replace the element below
  with individual <type fullname="..."/> entries for at least these types and their derived
  classes, and verify with `dotnet publish -p:PublishAot=true` that timings still populate.

  See: https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/core/deploying/trimming/trimming-options#root-descriptors
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="ZenStates-Core" preserve="all" />
</linker>
